                <!-- Annex 1 -->
                <div class="p-8 doc-section" id="annex-1">
                    <h2>Annex 1 — Data Processing Terms</h2>
                    <p><strong class="text-dark">1. Subject matter.</strong> This Annex sets out the terms required by
                        Article 28 GDPR for cases where the User (the <strong class="text-dark">Controller</strong>)
                        processes personal data through the Service and the Provider (the
                        <strong class="text-dark">Processor</strong>) carries out processing operations on the
                        Controller’s behalf.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">2. Nature and purpose of the processing.</strong>
                        Producing and publishing marketing content, compiling and sending newsletter campaigns,
                        processing webshop data, and the storage and technical operations necessary to provide the
                        Service.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">3. Duration of the processing.</strong> For the term of
                        the subscription, or until the Controller instructs deletion.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">4. Categories of data subjects.</strong> The
                        Controller’s newsletter subscribers, customers and contact persons, and persons appearing in
                        material uploaded by the Controller.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">5. Types of personal data.</strong> Name, e-mail
                        address, other fields present in the mailing list, likenesses appearing in uploaded media
                        files, and any other data provided by the Controller.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">6. Processing on instructions.</strong> The Processor
                        processes personal data solely on the documented instructions of the Controller — including
                        operations carried out through the interface of the Service — unless required to do otherwise
                        by Union or Member State law; in that case the Processor informs the Controller beforehand,
                        unless the law prohibits it.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">7. Confidentiality.</strong> The Processor ensures that
                        persons authorised to access the data have committed themselves to confidentiality.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">8. Security measures.</strong> The Processor applies the
                        measures required by Article 32 GDPR, in particular: storage of data within the EU;
                        per-user, database-level isolation (row-level security); encrypted storage of access keys and
                        tokens (AES-256-GCM); encrypted transmission (TLS); logging and access control; daily
                        backups.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">9. Sub-processors.</strong> The Controller gives general
                        authorisation for the engagement of sub-processors. The current list of sub-processors
                        engaged is available in Section 5 of the <a href={privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>. In the event of
                        a change, the Processor publishes a notice <strong class="text-dark">at least 30 days</strong>
                        in advance, against which the Controller may object; in the event of an objection the
                        Controller may terminate its subscription.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">10. Data subject rights.</strong> The Processor assists
                        the Controller in fulfilling data subject requests through the features of the Service and, if
                        needed, through reasonable cooperation. If such a request reaches the Processor, it forwards
                        the request to the Controller and does not fulfil it independently.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">11. Personal data breach.</strong> The Processor
                        notifies the Controller of any personal data breach it becomes aware of
                        <strong class="text-dark">without undue delay and no later than 48 hours</strong>, and
                        provides the information necessary for notification.</p>
                    <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-dark">12. Deletion or return.</strong> On termination of the
                        relationship the Processor deletes or returns the personal data at the Controller’s choice,
                        no later than <strong class="text-dark">within 30 days</strong>, unless retention is required
